# Entities Card & Entity Rows

<h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

An entities card is a titled list. Each line is a row for one entity, and Home Assistant picks the kind of row from the entity’s domain, so a light gets a switch and a sensor gets a reading. A few special rows add dividers, section labels, links and buttons. Use it for a short list of related things, such as everything in one room.

This page owns the card and every row. For how to mix readings, attributes and actions in one list, see [Entity lists, readings and row actions](../home-assistant/entity-lists-and-rows.html). For card structure, see [Card (Base Surface)](cards.html).

